WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:05.440
<i>The student council president tried to
mediate our troubles with the underclassman,</i>

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.470
<i>but for some reason that underclassman seems 
to have had a misunderstanding with the president.</i>

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.620
You covered for them because
you're just like them, didn't you?!

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:21.910
You pretended to be worried about me,
but you were just protecting yourself!

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:22.710
Nishimiya!

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.810
That was rather embarrassing.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.210
President.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:35.830
Thanks.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.640
So you like Sanrio, too.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:42.350
I had heard that the source
of your dispute with Nishimiya

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.280
was over interests, but
I didn't realize it was this.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.580
Man, I was seriously shocked, too.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.820
I'm not trying to hide it, but
I don't exactly talk about it either.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:55.650
But Nishimiya believed
you were hiding it from him.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.020
Seems so.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.260
Above the Distant Clouds

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.680
I want to help you.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.850
What a joke!

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:50.580
I'm leaving early.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.530
But you just got here.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.950
President, about my request
to use the gym from the other day.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.350
Minamoto, the archery club
match is starting soon.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.570
Hey, I was talking to him first.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.260
President, can I borrow your notes?

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.660
Wow...

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:08.650
Hey!

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.840
There's a bunch of people
surrounding the president's desk.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.120
Should we come back?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.210
All right, let me handle this.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.800
Miss, miss.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:20.530
Me?

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.990
Will you listen to my request?

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:23.960
Huh?

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:25.800
I'll make sure to repay you later.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.970
What's your request?

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.780
Can you listen to what the people
around the president's desk have to say

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.710
and take notes for me?

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:34.610
What?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.240
I'll treat you to lunch at school in return?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.970
And they'll join us, too.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.910
Okay, line up single file!

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.910
Are you always this busy?

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.610
They usually don't come all at
once, but this is pretty normal.

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:50.960
What do you need?

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.420
If it's about Nishimiya, I was
hoping you could wait a bit.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.000
About that, why don't you let us handle it?

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.050
We're the ones who started this
to begin with, so I'll talk to him.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:05.830
No, it's fine.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.860
I'll resolve what happened this morning myself,

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.810
you guys don't need to worry about it.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.850
And I also need to make
Nishimiya properly apologize.

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.090
But...

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.230
This morning's incident was my mistake.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.780
That's why I'll be the one to resolve it.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.320
President, I took notes for you.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:22.780
Here.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:23.970
Thanks.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:25.820
I look forward to my meal.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:30.580
About using the gym, I will have
to speak to the other clubs,

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.160
but if you submit a document
with your desired date and time...

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
<b>I guess that makes sense.</b>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
<b>Senpai, you haven't used 
Line very much, have you?</b>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
<b>Honestly, not mich.</b>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
It ended up as "mich".

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
<b>I need to talk to you
 about this morning.</b>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.260
<b>Won't you answer me?</b>

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:53.920
Go, Benkei!

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.730
It's morning, Seiichirou.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:09.790
You overslept?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.430
A person who cannot rule himself
cannot be called an adult.

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:14.900
My apologies.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.830
But that's unusual for you to
sleep longer than your alarm.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:24.550
He's right, that's probably the first
time I've ever heard your alarm.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.380
I will be more careful tomorrow.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.500
You're so stiff.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.060
Seiichirou's turned out so stiff
because you're so strict, Dad.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.220
I thought I raised you the same way.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.560
I take college quite seriously, you know.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.560
Are you okay though, Seiichirou-san?

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.080
Perhaps you're not feeling well
and that's why you overslept?

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:48.950
I'm fine! I just didn't get enough sleep.

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:50.840
Were you studying?

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:54.100
Or were you unable to sleep because
you were worried about something?

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.160
Oh, did something happen?

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.830
Nothing in particular!

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.510
Huh, he's not here.

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:10.270
Oh, are you looking for the handsome
boy who's usually here watching things?

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.860
It was my secret fun in the morning.

00:06:12.860 --> 00:06:14.310
I totally get it.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:15.430
Right?

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.850
Too bad. I wonder what happened to him?

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:26.360
Excuse me, but could you
get Nishimiya Ryo for me?

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.330
Ah, Nishimiya is absent today.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:32.880
I see, sorry for bothering you.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:49.630
<b>Senpai: Are you feeling all right?</b>

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:49.630
<b>Senpai: I want to clear up the misunderstanding
from yesterday. Will you meet with me?</b>

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:49.630
<b>Senpai: Please listen to what I have to say.</b>

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.310
Apparently Nishimiya-kun is absent today.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:06.230
What? Did you go down
to Nishimiya's class to check?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.070
I mean, doesn't it bother you?

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.860
Is it because of yesterday?

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.500
What are we going to do?

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:16.830
What can we do? 
The president rejected our help.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:34.620
Submitting paperwork?

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:38.680
You always submit your
class' paperwork so diligently.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.160
Thank you.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.200
How do you feel, Ryo-chan?

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.350
Not so good.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.400
I see.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.620
You have a visitor.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.280
I don't want to see anyone—

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:02.170
Who's here?

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:04.970
A boy named Minamoto Seiichirou-san.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:09.250
He's in the parlor, what should I do?

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:10.900
Should I have him leave?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.720
What a relief, you look well.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.650
What did you come here for?

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.590
I came to clear up a misunderstanding.

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:26.080
Misunderstanding?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.090
I knew that you and the others
quarreled over interests,

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:33.240
but I didn't know that it was about Sanrio.

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:38.250
And I wasn't trying to hide the
fact that I like Sanrio from you.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.290
You expect me to believe that?

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.250
I want you to believe it.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:48.760
My, my.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:52.540
Minamoto-san, please sit.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:53.780
You sit too, Ryo-chan.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:06.310
I don't know what happened,
but calm down and have some tea.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:09.570
Why did you pour it in that?

00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:15.780
But this Little Twin Stars
cup is your favorite, isn't it?

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.470
That was a long time ago!

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:19.080
I get it now.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:21.770
You really hate Sanrio, don't you?

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:22.820
I do hate it!

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.760
I'm sorry for bringing up unpleasant feelings.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.710
Minamoto-san?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:30.930
Yeah, that's right!

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.630
An apology will make it all better, right?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.300
Ryo-chan?

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.090
According to your reasoning.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.840
Okay then, that's good.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:41.070
You should apologize when you're in the wrong.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:45.550
But I can't forgive you.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:47.170
Why not?

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:51.300
Nishimiya?

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:55.060
You're perfect, so how could you
possibly understand how I feel?

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:56.860
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.450
It doesn't matter, just leave!

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.300
No, please explain it to me!

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.240
Even I don't understand it!

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:04.750
Nishimiya?

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:05.300
Leave!

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:14.210
I'm sorry that my son was so rude.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:18.180
No, I'm sorry for intruding so suddenly.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:31.230
<i>What does it mean?</i>

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.530
<i>Why can't I work this out?</i>

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:58.450
<i>What kind of student council president am I
if I can't even convince a single student?</i>

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.770
What's wrong? You don't look so good.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:19.430
You're probably right.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.430
Hey, are you okay?

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:24.660
I'm fine.

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:28.510
If things are busy with the student council,
you can take a break from morning practices.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:30.950
I'll look after the underclassmen.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:32.730
I'm really okay.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:41.690
I'm sorry, things with Nishimiya
still haven't been resolved.

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.470
About that...

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:47.230
Please let us help you, too.

00:11:47.230 --> 00:11:49.370
We can't just go on pretending
like we're clueless.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.280
So, it's like Kouta said.

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:52.300
Please.

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.500
I appreciate the sentiment, but I'm fine.

00:11:56.940 --> 00:12:01.970
It kind of made me sad when
you rejected our help earlier.

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:06.860
I'm sure you're just trying to look out for us,

00:12:07.710 --> 00:12:10.450
but it made me think you might not trust us.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:13.080
No, that wasn't my intention!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.490
I just feel like I want to finish what
I started and see it through myself.

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.540
That's just it though!

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:21.220
No matter how perfect you are, it's too much.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.570
And it makes us feel lonely.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:25.410
Because we're not perfect.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:30.530
You're perfect, so how could you
possibly understand how I feel?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.220
So that's what he meant?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.020
I finally understand now.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.610
Does that mean you'll let us help you?

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.010
Yes, please.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:47.200
Help me.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:48.700
We will!

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.840
Please leave it to us!

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.300
I like to shake hands with
Cinnamoroll at Puroland.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.970
So Cinnamoroll is your favorite.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.340
Yes.

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:15.060
Cinnamoroll's hands are so... warm...

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:22.740
President?!

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.990
I'll take him to the nurse's office.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.360
R-Right.

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.450
Nishimiya-kun? Is Nishimiya Ryo-kun here?

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.870
Wh-What do you want?

00:13:33.390 --> 00:13:35.150
The president collapsed just now.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:38.600
He's being carried to the nurse's
office right now, but you should—

00:13:38.600 --> 00:13:39.570
So what?

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.130
Why should I care?

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:46.970
Well, I just thought you should know...

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.090
Huh? I don't get you.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:49.890
But—

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:53.480
Whether he collapsed or not
has nothing to do with me, does it?

00:13:54.490 --> 00:13:58.300
He's in a different grade and
he's not exactly my friend,

00:13:58.790 --> 00:14:01.720
so why do I have to go see
him? I don't get it.

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.140
It does involve you!

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:07.800
You've been angry and absent ever since you
threw the president's student handbook at him,

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:09.910
how can you say it has nothing to do with you?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:13.670
Th-That's not why I was absent.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:18.950
He's been working hard to mend things
between us because of our dispute.

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:22.750
Even though he's busy,
he's been looking out for us.

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:25.630
I'm sure that includes you, too.

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:39.440
You asked us if we were ashamed
of ourselves in the library,

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.450
but I think you're the one who is even
more shameful for saying such things

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.270
when someone who has looked
after you has collapsed.

00:14:54.650 --> 00:14:58.230
1, 2, 3, 4.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.210
1, 2, 3, 4.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:06.570
1, 2, 3, 4.

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:06.090
<i>One day, when I was still just a kid...</i>

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.080
Seiichirou.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:10.550
Yes, sir.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:13.520
We're going out, so please get dressed.

00:15:13.520 --> 00:15:14.550
Y-Yes, sir.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:18.980
<i>Father took me with him without
mentioning where we were going.</i>

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.840
<i>And then we arrived at Sanrio Puroland.</i>

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:41.730
<i>I still remember the first
time I met Cinnamoroll.</i>

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:46.100
<i>I couldn't take my eyes
off him the moment I met him.</i>

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:07.070
<i>The moment I held his soft, warm hand,</i>

00:16:08.140 --> 00:16:10.690
<i>somehow I felt relieved and
all the tension left my body.</i>

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:14.070
<i>Next thing I knew, I was smiling.</i>

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.460
Kouta, where did you go?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.500
I thought I'd try to get Nishimiya-kun.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.760
Why him?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:38.380
I don't really know why either,
but I felt like I had to get him.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:43.330
But it was pointless, wasn't it?
That sourpuss ain't coming.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:45.600
Yeah, he said it had nothing to do with him.

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.710
Go figure.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:49.490
Doesn't seem to be the case.

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.740
Nishimiya-kun?

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.080
I don't like being ashamed of myself.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.200
Senpai!

00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:08.710
He's overworked and hasn't slept much.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:14.540
That's probably because he was dealing
with the archery club, the student council,

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:18.020
looking after classes, and on
top of that, trying to solve our dispute.

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:19.890
Of course he'd be overworked.

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.750
He even came to my house.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.270
Seriously?

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:30.550
Even though he's so busy,
he came just to apologize to me.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.640
But I went and turned him away.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:38.930
For me to say it has nothing to do
with me when he ends up like this...

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:42.020
I'm the worst.

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:44.570
I'm the one who's the worst.

00:17:46.570 --> 00:17:47.680
Senpai!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:48.710
Are you all right?

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.090
I just didn't get enough sleep.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.930
I guess I got a bit too focused on my studies.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:58.020
More importantly, why is Nishimiya here?

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.570
I asked for him.

00:18:00.570 --> 00:18:02.710
I see, that's perfect.

00:18:04.510 --> 00:18:05.790
President.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.250
Please don't overdo it.

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:08.630
I'm fine.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:10.870
Nishimiya.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:13.780
I'm sorry.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.210
Please stop, I'm the one who's at fault.

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:24.770
I've known that it's not your fault.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:28.690
Still though, I made you...

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:29.810
It's not about that.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:37.970
I told you to face yourself,
but I couldn't face myself.

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:45.250
I try to do everything so perfectly, to
avoid seeing that I can't rely on others.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:52.580
Because of that, I rely on Cinnamoroll
and go to Puroland seeking healing.

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.440
I'm really the worst.

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.570
That's not true, you were caring for me!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.850
I actually like Sanrio

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.170
and Little Twin Stars.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:12.500
Huh?!

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:14.090
So that's it?!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.840
Be quiet.

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:20.650
I thought that it wasn't very manly,

00:19:20.650 --> 00:19:25.050
but hearing Mizuno-senpai and the others
talking about Sanrio without a care in the world

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:28.430
irritated me, making me jealous and angry.

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:33.510
I like it, but I worry what people think

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:36.860
and got irritated and even lashed out at you.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:39.680
I'm sorry, I...

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:41.930
I...

00:21:31.230 --> 00:21:33.410
What nice weather.

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:36.050
Mornin' Kouta.

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:38.020
Morning Yuu, Shunsuke.

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:40.740
Are you sure this is the right time?

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.870
Have faith in my research skills. See.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:46.700
It's true.

00:21:47.720 --> 00:21:51.470
Morning President! Nice weather we're having.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.870
Ah, morning.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:54.590
It is lovely weather.

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:56.420
Are you feeling better?

00:21:56.420 --> 00:21:58.320
Thank you, I'm all right.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:00.530
We were worried about you.

00:22:00.530 --> 00:22:04.170
I took a break from club and council
activities yesterday and rested at home.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:07.170
You'll just have to keep playing hooky.

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:10.290
That will be difficult.

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:11.470
Senpai!

00:22:12.780 --> 00:22:14.160
Good morning.

00:22:14.630 --> 00:22:15.430
Morning.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:17.510
You're joining him now?

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:18.420
What of it?

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:19.300
Nothing.

00:22:21.670 --> 00:22:25.070
Senpai, may I come watch
the archery club after school?

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:27.700
Yes, of course.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:33.130
You two seem to have worked things out.

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:35.080
Will you be making up with us too then?

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.610
I'll take that bit by bit.

00:22:37.410 --> 00:22:39.620
What? You're not cute at all.

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:41.960
I don't want you to think I'm cute.

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:42.980
Why you!

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.050
Now, now.

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:47.550
Oh, finally bringing out the Sanrio stuff?

00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:51.260
<b>Factoid: A philosophical explanation book. For children,
it's like a picture book, but it's informative for adults.</b>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:50.500
It's just a normal library book.

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:53.370
A Little Twin Stars book?

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:54.170
Yeah.

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:55.970
His attitude has really changed.

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:00.100
Pompompurin,

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.040
My Melody,

00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:04.400
Hello Kitty,

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:06.970
Little Twin Stars,

00:23:08.540 --> 00:23:09.390
Cinnamoroll.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:14.680
All together, we're the Sanrio Boys.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:15.540
Now that you mention it...

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:17.470
Don't lump me in with you.

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:19.340
We must have some kind of connection.

00:23:19.340 --> 00:23:20.330
You're right.

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:22.320
You're even more cute now.

00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:24.790
Please don't call me cute!

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.770
<i>This was the beginning</i>

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>of our slightly strange and sparkling youth.</i>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:40.210
Next Episode

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:39.010
Next time, "Miraculous Holiday".
